  # v1.60.2, external review of 1.60.1: the data machine 4's rates are
  # read against, and the methods named in the code. The data's
  # licence and how EquiPop derived the table: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
  # v1.61.3 (BACKLOG 428): the licence is in `notes`, not `license:`.
  # CFF 1.2.0 accepts only its own snapshot of SPDX ids, and
  # CC-BY-3.0-IGO is not in it - the file failed its schema for two
  # releases while the check that says so skipped for want of cffconvert.
  - type: data
    title: "World Population Prospects 2024"
    authors:
      - name: "United Nations, Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division"
    year: 2024
    url: "https://population.un.org/wpp/"
    repository: "https://github.com/PPgp/wpp2024"
    notes: "Licence CC BY 3.0 IGO. Via the wpp2024 R package 1.1-3 (2024-11-26). EquiPop ships a derived table, equipop/data/wpp2024_reference.csv.xz, built by tools/make_wpp_reference.py."
  - type: article
    title: "Average age at death in infancy and infant mortality level: Reconsidering the Coale-Demeny formulas at current levels of low mortality"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Andreev"
        given-names: "Evgeny M."
      - family-names: "Kingkade"
        given-names: "W. Ward"
    journal: "Demographic Research"
